    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A P-trap is the U-shaped pipe beneath your sink that holds water to block sewer gases, and it usually sits on curved elbows with a single removable slip nut connecting to your vertical waste pipe. To inspect it, place rags over the bottom to catch water, then loosen the slip nut at the bottom with a worm gear wrench, set it aside, and clear out any debris or debris using a brush and cloth while watching for slow drain times. If the pipe inside the P-trap feels rough or has a distinct hairline crack visible, you may have a blockage or a leak that's too complex to fix yourself, so it's safer to call a professional.",
